The program of omp-target-receive-array.m, compiled by the driver for the
machine's GPU and run there: the callback copies each array into the
device's arena while the kernel runs.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/omp-target-receive-array.m -o %t.O2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY timeout -k 1 60 %t.O2 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %S/omp-target-receive-array.m --check-prefix=OUTPUT --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

The arrays that the region took from its ring are freed, as the host copies
each with its mailbox's lock held, so that no thread without a process reads
it.
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t.O2 2>&1 \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MESSAGES --match-full-lines
MESSAGES:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
